      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of being a hollowed-out shell is incredibly heavy, and it takes immense energy just to keep putting one foot in front of the other. If the past version of you is gone, perhaps the next step is to stop trying to revive that ghost and just accept the quiet exhaustion you feel right now. Sometimes the only thing left to do is to let the pressure drop, allowing yourself to just *be* in the void without the burden of pretending.",
      "source": "target",
